{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>And they embittered them, etc.</b> Its saying <b>with hard labor</b> means — with labor that is hard in and of itself even in small quantity from it, and that is the labor of mortar and bricks and field labor." "And its saying <b>all their labor</b> etc. — for you should not say that they relaxed their hand from them regarding the quota of building that they had previously fixed for them; rather, the original quota of labor stands in its place and they added to it. As you might say: after they imposed upon them so-and-so [bricks] that they must build each day, on condition that the mortar and the bricks be prepared before them, they added upon them to do the preparation of the mortar and the bricks and all the labor of preparing the building, and they did not lighten on this account any of the original quota of labor under which they had worked with rigor, but rather it remained along with it. And this was part of the cunning, lest [Israel] multiply; yet even so, it did not avail them to diminish them, for the children of Israel multiplied and sufficed for this matter, and therefore ״וַיֹּאמֶר מֶלֶךְ מִצְרַיִם״ etc. — to kill the males."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:23:02.461667323Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}